title: 'step 1: shuffle'
pid: 913353c2-aaa1-4cc6-8101-9ebf0af17d94
body: |2-
  Welcome, Codex! Please read coding-advice/ORIENTATION.org, and whatever it refers to (recursively), for orientation. (If anything refers to Claude in the present or future tense, please don't be offended. You are the chosen one, um, lately.)

  Then: This project has gotten too big. server/ has 43,000 lines of Rust code. It did almost everything it now does 20K lines ago. Every change is now a massive ordeal. Our mission is to reduce that complexity.

  But before we can even *surveil* it, we need to shuffle things. The codebase has been growing for 1.5 years. At some point I gave up and let AI do lots of things with much less oversight than I would like to give, and now concerns are extremely mixed across files.

  So I would like you to make a plan, which I will review, to move functions across files until each collection feels coherent.

  You might find the call-graph and code-map tools at tools/introspect/ helpful. (You'll certainly want that kind of information, but maybe not in that format.)

  Please put your results in a new headline below this one.
